cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CBS3D++ in research, cite the software repository and the
  numerical references relevant to the configuration used.
title: "CBS3D++: A finite-element-based fluid dynamics solver"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bharadwaj
    given-names: Prajwal
repository-code: "https://github.com/prajwal1798/CBS-3D"
url: "https://github.com/prajwal1798/CBS-3D"
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - finite element method
  - incompressible flow
  - characteristic-based split
  - conjugate heat transfer
  - multiphysics
  - parallel computing
abstract: >-
  CBS3D++ is a C++20 finite-element solver for three-dimensional
  incompressible fluid dynamics. It uses a semi-implicit
  Characteristic-Based Split pressure-projection formulation on linear
  tetrahedral elements and includes active development for multiphysics,
  turbulence modelling and distributed-memory parallel execution.
